{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790383206,"nonce":"3D/P782YMQB5HrscBDZMq6CqKbw=","title":"Value representation lost across calls: inliner retyping, virtual defaults, reflect, Dynamic ++, Int with Int64","message":"From a triage of 16 WRONG_ANSWER rows that printed pointers or raw bits (four read-only subagents, probes under scratch triage-a..d). Fixed here:\n\n- Issue10752: the MIR inliner mapped a callee parameter onto the caller's argument register and then copied the callee's parameter type (I64 for an erased T) onto that CALLER register, so `show(1 \u003c\u003c 33)` / `show(big + one)` became i64 ops with no 32-bit wrap. The caller's register now keeps its type; a narrower integer (or Bool) argument widens into its own register.\n- Exposed by that: TestInt64 passed only because `int64eq`'s `==` compared truncated 32-bit values. `Int - Int64` / `Int + Int64` were computed in 32 bits (build_binop typed the result from the LEFT operand; the Int64 `@:op` is looked up on the left type only). build_binop now sign-extends the I32 side when the other is I64 (not for shifts).\n- Issue11666: try_virtual_dispatch never filled default arguments.\n- Issue2272: runtime raw_value_to_slot wrote a box address into a scalar field slot; a scalar-tagged box now stores its payload.\n- Issue2308: Reflect.callMethod passed the args array to ANY one-parameter function held in a local; now only when that parameter is an Array.\n- Issue7335: `++`/`--` on a Dynamic lvalue did integer add on the box pointer; now haxe_dynamic_arith.\n- Issue8242: `Null\u003cInt\u003e - 1` was typed Float (default arm); a nullable primitive operand now types as its primitive.\n- Issue6703: `inst.m` on an interface receiver was an unresolved field (E0100); now a closure forwarding through an interface call.\n\nResult: report-cb 696 (from 689), 0 LOST. Suite 206/0/2, fixtures, compiler integration tests and runtime tests green. Fixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/ValueShapesAcrossCalls.hx.\n\nTriage findings NOT fixed here (filed or still open): b3220bf (structural receivers bind by bare name), 14e397f, 456a69c; Issue2639 generic @:from, Issue2685 @:to at call args, Issue2767 inliner Array receiver, Issue2914 switch capture over Null\u003cInt\u003e untyped, Issue3214 user Int64 merges with haxe.Int64, Issue4740, Issue5124 Int literal into Float-bound T, Issue8740 entry-file double compile skips unbox, TestConstrainedMonomorphs field GEP on constrained T.","files":null}]}